Subject: [PATCH 17/30] ui/console: allow CPU listeners with GL presentation

GTK and SDL attach a GL context even when a software adapter such as
VMware SVGA supplies a CPU framebuffer. The unconditional context check
then rejects VNC, although it can consume that framebuffer directly.

Require context compatibility when the guest requires GL rendering or
when the listener has GL update callbacks. Keep GL-context and DMABUF
requirements intact. This allows accelerated local presentation and VNC
for software framebuffers; it does not provide GPU texture readback for
GTK/SDL guests using virgl.

Validated with raw VNC pixel comparison, mode changes and reconnects
under GTK/Wayland, GTK/X11 with Xvfb and SDL. Guest GL rendering still
rejects VNC. OPENSTEP also boots with GTK GL and VNC together.

---
diff --git a/ui/console.c b/ui/console.c
index a8a2a24..3eca4ee 100644
--- a/ui/console.c
+++ b/ui/console.c
@@ -572,7 +572,12 @@ static bool console_compatible_with(QemuConsole *con,
 
     flags = con->hw_ops->get_flags ? con->hw_ops->get_flags(con->hw) : 0;
 
+    /* A GL context may only be used to present a software framebuffer.
+     * Such a console can still be shared with CPU display listeners (VNC,
+     * for example). Context compatibility matters for guest GL rendering.
+     */
     if (qemu_console_has_gl(con) &&
+        ((flags & GRAPHIC_FLAGS_GL) || dcl->ops->dpy_gl_update) &&
         !con->gl->ops->dpy_gl_ctx_is_compatible_dcl(con->gl, dcl)) {
         error_setg(errp, "Display %s is incompatible with the GL context",
                    dcl->ops->dpy_name);
